    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the registration-date behavior with a small, localized footprint.\n\n**Behavior:** When an owner is created without a `registrationDate`, it defaults to the server's current date; a supplied date is kept. The field is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format (native `LocalDate` serialization via the OpenAPI `format: date` mapping).\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it flows through the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (input) and `OwnerDto` (output). MapStruct auto-maps it by name, so the mapper needed no changes.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field with getter/setter and a small, cohesive `@PrePersist` hook (`ensureRegistrationDate`, CC 2) that defaults a null value to `LocalDate.now()`. Keeping the default in a new tiny method rather than editing existing ones avoids paying the class's WMC on complex code.\n- **Schema files** (all four DBs) \u2014 added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n- **`hsqldb`/`mysql` `data.sql`** \u2014 appended a `NULL` to the positional owner seed inserts to match the new column count (h2/postgres seeds already use explicit column lists and were unaffected).\n\nNo existing method's logic was modified; the new behavior is confined to one small entity method plus schema/data adjustments.",
